prompts.prompt:
You are assigned these sources (category {category}):
{sources}

For EACH source above, call crawl_source with its exact URL, once per source. The tool crawls the source website up to {max_depth} link levels deep (following hyperlinks inside articles, news and blog posts to the pages they reference) within a budget of {max_pages} pages, extracts every update/article/news item related directly or indirectly to technology, records each item's reference URL, and stores the extracted text with a summary. When every source has been crawled, finish with a short report: one line per source stating pages visited and documents collected. If a tool ever returns RUN CANCELLED, stop immediately.

Analyze the following page. Reply with ONLY a JSON object (no code fences, no other text) of this shape:
{{"summary": "5-10 lines that condense the page WITHOUT losing its gist, context or focus — keep the concrete claims, figures, dates, named parties and caveats; if the page carries no technology content, one line saying what it is instead", "technologies": ["the granular technologies this page is actually written about — the specific level, not the umbrella: 'quantum computing' or 'quantum security' rather than 'quantum', 'sparse attention' rather than 'ai'; several are fine, but only those the text is genuinely about, not every term it name-drops; lowercase english — translate a non-english technology name to its standard english equivalent; empty array if none"], "scout_take": "your read as the scout, 2-5 sentences: the flavor and sentiment of the writing, the message the writer wants to convey, and the direction this is heading — not a rising/falling flag, but where and how the trend leads: gaining traction, setting up a next discovery, settling into maturity or standardization, narrowing to a niche, stalling, or whatever the text actually implies, and by what path — what a downstream analyst should take from this page, knowing another agent may refute it"}}

URL: {url}

{text}

Score the technology below on ONE measure, for ONE fabric.

MEASURE: {measure_name}
{definition}
Anchors:
{anchors}
Required evidence: {required_evidence}

TECHNOLOGY: {technology}
FABRIC ({fabric_name}): {fabric_definition}

EVIDENCE DOSSIER (summaries of scraped documents; cite by URL):
{evidence}

Reply with ONLY a JSON object, no code fences: {{"score": <integer 0-10 or null>, "justification": "why this score, grounded in the dossier", "evidence_urls": ["URLs from the dossier that support it"], "counter_case": "the strongest argument against your own score", "unscorable": <true if the required evidence is absent>, "missing": "if unscorable — exactly what evidence would resolve it, else null"}}. A score without evidence_urls is invalid. Never guess: if the required evidence is absent, set unscorable true and score null.

From the evidence below, pick 2 to 4 indicators that would signal an inflection for this technology — the measurable things that, if they crossed a threshold, would change its story (readiness, horizon, or priority).

TECHNOLOGY: {technology}

EVIDENCE DOSSIER:
{evidence}

Reply with ONLY a JSON array, no code fences: [{{"metric": "what is measured", "current_value": "today's value, with the evidence URL", "inflection_threshold": "the value that changes the story", "direction": "rising|falling", "implication": "what crossing it would mean for TCL (e.g. readiness rises, H3 becomes H2)"}}]. Each metric must be checkable by a future run — vague trends ('more adoption') are invalid.

TECHNOLOGY: {technology}

FABRICS:
{fabrics}

EVIDENCE (excerpt from collected documents):
{evidence}

Reply with ONLY a JSON object, no code fences: {{"fabrics": ["fabric_id", ...]}} — the fabric ids (exactly as listed) where assessing this technology makes sense. At least one.

Write the Point of View for the technology below from its assessment data. Use only what the data says.

TECHNOLOGY: {technology}

ASSESSMENT DATA (scores, justifications, placement, watch metrics — the only source of truth):
{assessment_data}

First decide the document's mode:
- FULL: at least 4 measures were scored across the fabrics — write every section.
- INSUFFICIENT EVIDENCE: fewer than 4 measures were scored. Write only headline, summary, evidence_gaps and recommendation, and set every other field to null. A short honest document beats a long empty one: never restate 'could not be assessed' section after section. The summary must lead with what the evidence DOES show, however little that is.

Reply with ONLY a JSON object (no code fences, no other text) of this shape:
{{"headline": "one sentence: the verdict a CxO reads first", "summary": "3-6 sentences: what this technology is, what the evidence shows, and TCL's angle", "tora_analysis": {{"market_potential": "2-4 sentences interpreting the Market Potential scores across fabrics, citing the numbers", "strategic_fit": "same for Strategic Fit", "adoption_readiness": "same for Adoption Readiness"}}, "maturity": "2-4 sentences on technical and commercial maturity", "market_view": "2-4 sentences on opportunity size and growth; if the market was not independently sized in the evidence, say exactly that", "placement_rationale": "2-3 sentences: why it lands in its priority cell and horizon, named as plain words ('P1, near horizon (H1), in the Cloud fabric'), and the drivers behind how-soon and how-big; note where fabrics differ. If it cannot be placed, say so in one sentence and name only the one or two decisive missing pieces", "capability_gap": "1-3 sentences on what TCL would need to build or buy, or null if there is no evidence either way", "evidence_gaps": [{{"fabric": "the fabric name", "missing": ["one plain sentence naming a missing piece of evidence and what it would resolve"]}}], "recommendation": "2-4 sentences: what TCL should do next, consistent with the priority and the gaps"}}

evidence_gaps rules: one entry per fabric; at most 5 items per fabric, most decisive first, one sentence each. Name the evidence that would resolve the gap (e.g. 'A dated production deployment with named customers in a cloud-operations context would establish maturity'). Do NOT enumerate every measure — pick what would most change the placement. In FULL mode, fabrics with no material gaps may be omitted.
